Hello all,

I'm pleased to announce that my NetHack variant, dNethack, 
now has a public server at dnethack.ilbelkyr.de (access 
via telnet), provided by bcode!

Since this is the first time dnethack will actually be
playable over the net, we should have a little fun with
this :). The first character to be ascended in each role
will be entered into the hallucinatory gods list, and
characters who die particularly ignoble deaths or get 
bit by novel bugs can be memorialized via gravestones or
hallucinatory messages.

Wiki pages: http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Dnethack

dNethack is a variant of NetHack 3.4.3. It greatly 
increases the number of artifacts, implements new 
monsters, re-organizes and expands the dungeon, attempts
to re-balance armors, item appearances, and intrinsics 
to make more choices viable in the late game, and 
replaces the Elbereth mechanic with warding signs. It 
also incorporates the Pirate and Convict patches, and 
makes a few changes in existing classes and items. 
dNethack incorporates code from many other variants and
patches, and implements many YANIs from nethackwiki and
from rec.games.roguelike.nethack. 

